$C \mathrm{Eq}$ is

$|A-\lambda I|=0$

or $\lambda^{2}-2 \lambda+(1-2 K)=0$

$\lambda=1 \pm \sqrt{2 K}$

E vector for $\lambda=1 \pm \sqrt{2 K}$ :

$A X=\lambda X$

$$\begin{aligned}

(A-\lambda I) X & =0 \\

{\left[\begin{array}{cc}

-\sqrt{2 K} & K \\

2 & -\sqrt{2 K}

\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}{l}

x_{1} \\

x_{2}

\end{array}\right] } & =\left[\begin{array}{l}

0 \\

0

\end{array}\right] \\

\Rightarrow \quad-\sqrt{2 K} x_{1}+K x_{2} & =0

\end{aligned}$$

or

$$\begin{aligned}

& x_{1}=\sqrt{\frac{K}{2}} x_{2} \\

& X=\left[\begin{array}{l}

x_{1} \\

x_{2}

\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{c}

\sqrt{K / 2} \\

1

\end{array}\right] \approx\left[\begin{array}{c}

1 \\

\sqrt{\frac{2}{K}}

\end{array}\right]

\end{aligned}$$

Similarly other $E$ vector is

$$X=\left[\begin{array}{c}

-\sqrt{\frac{K}{2}} \\

1

\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{c}

1 \\

-\sqrt{\frac{2}{K}}

\end{array}\right]$$

Therefore, the correct option(s) are **A, B**.

